# macOS clutter
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes

# Claude Code local settings
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/launch.json

# Editor scratch
*.swp
*~

# Python's compiled leftovers, from running the preview server
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Raw video masters. Only the small web-ready .mp4 copies belong on the
# site. Masters are huge — over GitHub's 100 MB file limit, which fails
# the whole push — and publishing one would put the full-quality
# original at a public address.
assets/video/*.mov

# The album sleeve's full-size original — 2000px square and 5 MB, where
# the page shows it at 400px. The web copy beside it, album-cover.jpg,
# is the same picture at 216 KB and is what the site loads. Keeping the
# original here is useful; publishing it would put 5 MB in front of
# every visitor on a phone. Same bargain as the video masters above.
assets/img/album-cover.png

# Eric's tap-along tool for timing lyrics. It runs by double-clicking it
# and never needs to be online, so it stays on his computer instead of
# being published with the site.
tools/lyric-timer.html

# Notes written for Eric, not for visitors. Anything committed here is
# served publicly at graymanmusical.com/<filename>, and these two carry
# the access password and the weather key.
READ-ME-FIRST.txt
cloudflare/HOW-TO-DEPLOY.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# The album itself. THIS IS THE IMPORTANT ONE.
#
# These files used to live here and be published with the site, which
# meant anyone who knew the address could download the whole album
# without ever meeting the password — and so could anyone reading this
# public repository. On 29 September 2026 they were taken out of the
# repo and out of every commit in its history, and moved into private
# storage at Cloudflare that only the vault relay can read.
#
# They are still in these folders on Eric's own computer, which is
# where he works and what the local preview server reads. They are
# simply never committed again. Putting one back in the repo would
# publish it to the whole world and undo the lot.
#
# To add or replace a track or a lyric: put the file in the folder as
# usual, and ask Claude to put it in the vault as well. See CLAUDE.md,
# "The vault".
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# IGNORE EVERYTHING IN THESE FOLDERS, then allow back the one note
# explaining what goes in each. Listing extensions instead — which is
# what this did until 2 October 2026 — is one keystroke from publishing
# the album: the rule read "assets/notes/*.md", Eric's eighteen liner
# notes arrived as .txt, and all eighteen were staged for commit before
# anything caught it. They are personal writing about his own life. The
# same hole was open for any audio that was not .mp3.
#
# A folder listed here holds Eric's private material and the only thing
# in it that may ever be published is the PUT-…-HERE note. Deny first,
# allow by name.
assets/audio/*
!assets/audio/PUT-AUDIO-FILES-HERE.txt
assets/lyrics/*
!assets/lyrics/PUT-LYRICS-HERE.txt
assets/notes/*
!assets/notes/PUT-NOTES-HERE.txt
assets/downloads/*
!assets/downloads/PUT-DOWNLOAD-FILES-HERE.txt
